                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Digital Object Identifier (DOI) is a centrally registered identifier that provides a unique, persistent reference to digital objects such as publications, datasets, and software, ensuring reliable access and citation." .


###  https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/NFDI_0001102
<https://nfdi.fiz-karlsruhe.de/ontology/NFDI_0001102> rdf:type owl:Class ;
